.TH SUM 1 "March 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sum \- compute legacy checksums and block counts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sum
.RB [ \-o " 1|2 ]"
.RB [ \-a " algorithm ]"
.RB [ \-s " string ]"
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-\-sysv ]
.RB [ \-\-algorithm= algorithm ]
.RB [ \-\-compat= "bsd|gnu ]"
.RI [ file ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sum
utility computes historic checksums and block counts.
.PP
With no
.I file
operands, input is read from standard input.
A
.I file
operand of
.B -
also means standard input.
.PP
Default behavior uses historic algorithm 1 (BSD rotate checksum)
with block counts rounded up in 1024-byte units.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " 1|2"
Select historic algorithm 1 (BSD rotate checksum) or 2 (SysV folding sum).
.TP
.B \-\-sysv
Select historic algorithm 2 (equivalent to
.BR \-o " 2").
.TP
.BI \-a " algorithm"
Add an algorithm selection. Supported names: old1, old2, bsd, sysv, 1, 2.
Multiple
.B \-a
or
.B \-\-algorithm
options may be specified.
.TP
.BI \-\-algorithm= "algorithm"
Unified algorithm selector. Same accepted values as
.BR \-a .
.TP
.BI \-\-compat= "bsd|gnu"
Set short-option conflict behavior.
Default is
.BR bsd .
.TP
.BI \-s " string"
In BSD compatibility mode, checksum the literal
.IR string .
In GNU compatibility mode, select the SysV algorithm.
.TP
.B \-r
In BSD compatibility mode, requests reverse output format for digest-style
algorithms (legacy sum algorithms remain unchanged).
In GNU compatibility mode,
.B \-r
selects the BSD algorithm.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode; print checksum only.
.TP
.B \-p
Echo bytes read from standard input to standard output while checksumming.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
For single-algorithm legacy output, each line is:
.PP
.RS
.I checksum blocks
.RI [ filename ]
.RE
.PP
When more than one algorithm is selected, output lines are prefixed with
the algorithm tag (
.B old1
or
.BR old2 ).
.SH CONFORMING TO
The
.B sum
utility follows BSD-first conflict policy when GNU and BSD flags overlap.
GNU long-option compatibility is provided for
.BR \-\-sysv ,
.BR \-\-help ,
and
.BR \-\-version .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The
.B sum
utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cksum (1)
